  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 207 AM CDT Wed Sep 9 2026\n\nIncreasing southwest winds today ahead of an approaching cold\nfront will push high temperatures into the 94 to 101 degree\nrange. With dew points in the lower to middle 70s, heat indices\nwill reach 102 to near 110 degrees, and a Heat Advisory is in\neffect from late this morning until early evening.\n\nModels show a cold front moving through the middle Mississippi\nand lower Ohio valleys late tonight through Thursday. Scattered\nshowers and thunderstorms are possible as early as midday today\n(20-40% chances), with chances by late tonight increasing to \n60-90% north to 30-50% south. As front pushes through the PAH \nforecast area Thursday, the highest chances will become focused \nacross our southern half of counties by late Thursday afternoon \nthrough Thursday night. \n\nSPC has expanded the Marginal Risk of severe thunderstorms today\nacross all of the PAH forecast area except southern portions of\nthe Pennyrile region. There is a Day 2 Marginal Risk across\nsouthern Missouri, far west Kentucky and extreme southern\nIllinois. Damaging wind gusts are the main concern with storms\nboth days. \n\nModels show the front lifting back to the northeast Friday into\nFriday night. The model blend produces 20-40% chances of \nshowers and storms Friday into Friday evening. Things remain\nunsettled into the weekend, with 20-40% chances of showers and\nstorms Saturday afternoon through Saturday night, and 20%\nchances during the day Sunday. Dry conditions are expected\nSunday night into Monday, then models show an approaching cold\nfront Tuesday producing shower and storm chances into at least\nmid week. \n\nAfter a brief return of near seasonal temperatures Friday, \nwinds shifting back to the south will push temperatures back to \nwell above normal with highs mostly in the lower 90s over the \nweekend, and the lower to middle 90s Monday.",
